  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International recorded $2.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International won 821 awards so far this fiscal year, and the average award size is $3M. Science Applications International obligations fell 45.0% year over year. Science Applications International obligations in FY26 to date are smaller than prior fiscal years, which include $4.5B in FY24 and $4.4B in FY23 and FY25. Science Applications International receives the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations from the Department of Defense and the General Services Administration, which obligated $960M and $897M respectively. Science Applications International sells primarily engineering and IT services, with Engineering Services accounting for $949M and Computer Systems Design Services accounting for $797M in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International also holds research and development awards, including $201M in physical, engineering, and life sciences R&D. Science Applications International’s current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of Science Applications International this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $960M to Science Applications International in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $897M. The Department of the Treasury, Department of Transportation, and Department of Commerce follow with $128M, $107M, and $70.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Science Applications International’s obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for Science Applications International at $949M in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services is next at $797M. Science Applications International also records R&D obligations, including $201M and $150M in two separate research and development categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International has $2.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International has 821 awards this fiscal year and the average award size is $3M. Science Applications International obligations fell 45.0% year over year, and prior-year totals include $4.5B in FY24 and $4.4B in FY23 and FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "Science Applications International’s largest buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Defense and the General Services Administration. The Department of Defense obligated $960M and the General Services Administration obligated $897M. Other buying agencies include the Department of the Treasury at $128M and the Department of Transportation at $107M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Science Applications International sells engineering and information technology services and research and development to the government. Engineering Services accounts for $949M and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $797M in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International also has R&D obligations of $201M and $150M in two research categories."
    },
